{"name":"Rooster Comb","hex":"#96463f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rooster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male domestic chicken (Gallus gallus domesticus) or other gallinaceous bird.","A bird or bat which roosts or is roosting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rooster"},{"term":"comb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A toothed implement:\nA toothed implement for grooming the hair or (formerly) for keeping it in place.\n\nA machine used in separating choice cotton fibers from worsted cloth fibers.\nThe toothed plate at the top and bottom of an escalator that prevents objects getting trapped between the moving stairs and fixed landings.\nA toothed tool used for chasing screws on work in a lathe; a chaser.\nThe notched scale of a wire micrometer.\nThe collector of an electrical machine, usually resembling a comb.\nA toothed plate used for creating wells in agar gels for electrophoresis.\n A toothed wooden pick used to push the weft thread tightly against the previous pass of thread to create a tight weave.\nOne of a pair of peculiar organs on the base of the abdomen in scorpions, with which they comb substrate.\nA ctene.","A toothed implement for grooming the hair or (formerly) for keeping it in place."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Especially of hair or fur, to groom with a toothed implement, especially a comb.","To separate choice cotton fibers from worsted cloth fibers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rooster Comb","blocks":[{"text":"Rooster Comb is a prominent ridge located in Henry W. Coe State Park, east of Morgan Hill, California and in Stanislaus County. Its name refers to the large fleshy red skin atop a rooster's head. The resemblance to a rooster's comb is evident by the large rock formations running the length of the ridge, separating it from the grassy slopes below. This contrast gives the illusion of a rooster's comb."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rooster_Comb","wikidata":"Q7366528"},{"title":"Chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The chicken is the domesticated form of the red junglefowl, originally native to Southeast Asia. It was first domesticated around 8,000 years ago and is one of the most common and widespread domesticated animals in the world. Chickens are primarily kept for their meat and eggs, though they are also kept as pets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken","wikidata":"Q780"},{"title":"Comb","blocks":[{"text":"A comb is a tool consisting of a shaft that holds a row of teeth for pulling through the hair to clean, untangle, or style it. Combs have been used since prehistoric times, having been discovered in very refined forms from settlements dating back to 5,000 years ago in Persia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Plastic_comb%2C_2015-06-07.jpg/330px-Plastic_comb%2C_2015-06-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comb","wikidata":"Q23834"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-500px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-500px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.